---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="A relaxed developer publication about everyday software problems, small experiments, and useful tools."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>A quiet corner for curious developers.</h1>
      <p>Something useful to read while your coffee cools.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="page-body">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>One idea at a time</h2>
        <p>
          Code Coffee Break explores the small decisions inside software. What
          does a timeout tell you? Why do cache misses arrive together? What
          makes a command pleasant to use?
        </p>
        <p>
          A good read leaves you with an example you can explain, a question to
          take back to your code, or a tool that helps you work something out.
        </p>
        <h2>Examples you can inspect</h2>
        <p>
          The opening articles are original, AI-assisted editorial pieces. They
          use fictional scenarios, source links, and runnable examples where
          appropriate. They are not accounts of personal projects or production
          incidents. Each article identifies its authorship and any illustrative
          data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Future contributors keep their own bylines. Measurements need a
          method; external claims need a source. Corrections should explain what
          changed.
        </p>
        <h2>Room for other voices</h2>
        <p>
          This begins as a small reading room. The{' '}
          <a href="/contribute">contribution guide</a> is ready; submissions are
          not open yet. There are no invented members, event schedules, or
          audience numbers.
        </p>
        <h2>Keep it simple</h2>
        <p>
          Read without an account. Try the <a href="/tools">browser tools</a>{' '}
          without uploading your inputs. Follow new writing through{' '}
          <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>. Coffee is the atmosphere, and there is no
          shop to browse.
        </p>
      </article>
      <Newsletter />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
